  <h2>What each component does</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Function</th><th>What to inspect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Rotor / disc</th><td>Rotates with the wheel and provides the friction surfaces.</td><td>Thickness, scoring, cracking, heat damage, corrosion and runout where specified.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Brake pads</th><td>Friction material presses against both rotor faces.</td><td>Remaining material, uneven wear, contamination and correct axle/application.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Caliper and piston</th><td>Hydraulic pressure moves the piston and applies the pads.</td><td>Leaks, binding, damaged boots and uneven pad wear.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Caliper carrier</th><td>Supports and locates the caliper relative to the rotor.</td><td>Corrosion, damaged threads, correct hardware and secure mounting.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Hydraulic hose</th><td>Transfers brake fluid pressure to the moving caliper.</td><td>Cracks, abrasion, leaks, twists and routing.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Dust shield</th><td>Helps protect the brake area from road debris.</td><td>Contact with rotor, corrosion and damage.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>2021 S60 brake hardware is not one universal setup</h2>
  <p>Brake diameter, caliper carrier, pads and hardware can vary with engine, drivetrain, wheel/brake option, comfort-pad specification and Polestar Engineered equipment. A generic drawing cannot identify the parts installed on a particular S60.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm front versus rear axle.</li>
    <li>Confirm the vehicle's brake package using VIN-specific parts information.</li>
    <li>Compare rotor diameter and thickness, pad shape, caliper and carrier before ordering.</li>
    <li>Check whether the selected rear-brake procedure requires an electronic parking-brake service mode.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For a visual parts-catalogue reference, see the <a href="https://www.volvopartscounter.com/v-2021-volvo-s60--t5-inscription--2-0l-l4-gas/brakes--brake-components">2021 S60 T5 Inscription brake-components catalogue</a>. It is a secondary retailer catalogue and must not replace a VIN-confirmed Volvo parts lookup.</p>

  <h2>Service safety</h2>
  <p>Brakes are safety-critical. This page is not a pad or rotor replacement procedure. Use the exact Volvo service instructions for the vehicle, including approved parts, one-time-use fasteners, torque values, brake-fluid handling, caliper support, and electronic parking-brake steps. Do not work beneath a vehicle supported only by a jack. If the pedal feels abnormal, fluid is leaking, or braking performance changes, do not continue driving.</p>

  <p><a href="../front-brake-pads/">Front brake pad replacement notes</a>.</p>
  <h2>2026 brake service cost reference</h2>
  <p>RepairPal estimates pad replacement for a 2021 S60 at <strong>$293–$350</strong> before tax/fees. If rotors are also required, use <strong>$500–$900 per axle</strong> as a broad planning allowance, not a confirmed price for every brake package. Request a VIN-based quote that identifies pad and rotor part numbers. <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/brake-pad-replacement-cost">RepairPal 2021 S60 brake-pad estimate</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
